WEBVTT

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.920
Vapor pressure stabilized.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.920
It should work this time.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.000
Right! Open the valve!

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.170
At last.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.420
At last, we've done it!

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.380
Now the Kingdom can finally crush the Commonwealth!

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.580
Long live the Kingdom of Albion!

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.250
Now we just have to work on mass production.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.000
You'll see what you get for stealing our country!

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.960
What's our target?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.250
A C-ball.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.960
The Kingdom has successfully
miniaturized the Cavorite control unit.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.790
I would like your team to take the prototype from them.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:24.250
So the main players in this shadow war
are the spies and the scientists.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.080
The Kingdom possesses
refining technology that we lack.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.250
If they combine it with the miniature control unit,

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.380
they would make large-scale gravity weapons a reality.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.380
If not handled carefully, this could change history.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.540
Isn't this a bit much for a team with amateurs?

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.500
Our more experienced spies could...

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:46.290
This is something only your team can do.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.130
Because of Princess?

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.920
She is your team's strong point.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:00.630
You will use her position to infiltrate
the ceremony at the Cavorite mine.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.130
Honestly, the way you work that princess...

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.710
Another thing, Dorothy...

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.540
This is for your ears only.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.130
Beatrice, switch.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:35.880
Checkmate.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.500
Your turn, Beatrice.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.330
You won't shake me this time.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.290
You keep saying that,
and yet you have lost ten times in a row.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.000
You've been losing right along with me, Miss Chise.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.830
I have been victorious once.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.460
It doesn't count as winning
when you cut down a police officer.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.290
Fear not. I used the back of my sword.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.330
And that makes it better?

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.420
Indeed it does.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.880
Say, I've been thinking.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.330
You don't suppose our team could use a name, do you?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.880
That's a wonderful idea!

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.790
They do say names and natures often agree.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.920
We don't need a team name.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.170
We don't want to make up any information
that could turn up as evidence.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.830
That's an ironclad spy rule.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:25.000
Is that why you tell nothing but lies?

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:29.130
If I'm a liar, then there's no point
in questioning me, is there?

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.630
We're all girls, so I think we should have a cute name.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.580
Something pink, or a flower.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:38.250
What about the name of that unusual bird
we saw the other day?

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.710
I think it was a penguin?

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:41.960
Just a moment.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.290
I'll do an onomancy reading for that name.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.880
This is the Security Service!

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.250
Open the door!

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:49.250
Welcome back, Dorothy.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.420
You could be a little scared, Partner.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.580
Did you get to see L?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.500
Yes, and he gave us the most annoying target.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.290
And you?

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.210
We were thinking of team names.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.630
We were practicing tailing.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.130
Ooh, team names, is it?

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.290
All right, I'll be Scotch, Ange will be Calvados,

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.080
Princess will be Champagne...

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:14.380
Chise, let's see...

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.170
They're all the names of liquors, aren't they?
Chise, let's see...

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:16.710
They're all the names of liquors, aren't they?

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.960
Don't be a part of this, Dorothy.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.790
They need to learn basic tailing techni-

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:21.790
Oh no!

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:26.290
How do I count the strokes
of the letters in your alphabet?

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.580
It's like a mechanical fortress.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.250
Cavorite is the heart and soul of Albion's Air Fleet.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:41.710
Naturally, the mines will be heavily guarded.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.630
Excuse me.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.000
Are you here for the ceremony?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.500
Hello, there.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.500
Princess!

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.420
I brought some friends from school with me.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:58.960
Is that all right?

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.920
I beg your pardon.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.960
Any friends of yours are welcome.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.540
The power of a nation's princess.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:12.170
If they tried to body check her, heads would roll.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:13.710
So I'm a key, then?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.630
Yes, a magic one.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.250
The ceremony starts in 30 minutes.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:32.710
With guests arriving and preparations underway,
this will be their busiest time.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.420
In other words, the time when security is the most lax.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:40.880
And we'll use that time to get the prototype
from the underground laboratory!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.460
You all know the plan, right?

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:47.040
Dorothy, Beatrice, and I will infiltrate the facility.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.080
Welcome, Princess.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.460
Her Majesty the Queen is here.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:53.580
If you'd be so kind...

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:54.790
Of course.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:58.750
Princess, we'll be a-waitin' right over there.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.380
I'm leaving Chise here to protect you.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.380
She's our most reliable fighter.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.420
One guard.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.670
What do we do?

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.250
Looks like I'm up.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.040
Um, just wh-what are you...?

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.580
Huh?

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.830
Another dead end?

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.830
You can take the stairs to the right.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.420
Then go straight ahead to the ceremony hall.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.630
Thanks f'r the directions!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.540
I think I drank too much.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.170
Could you get me something to drink?

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.420
I-if water will suffice.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.580
Oh, you're so kind!

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.000
Wh..what are you-?

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:11.540
You have such a cute face, Mr. Guard Man.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.420
Do... do you really... think so?

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:23.830
What the...?

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.330
Hey!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.330
Is that you, Jake?

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.670
There's been a methane explosion!

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:33.330
So that's where the dust is coming from!

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:34.830
I'll take over here!

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.790
You go get some masks!

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.290
They're in Storeroom Three.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.210
Three? That's all the way on the other side!

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.880
Give me a break!

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:46.000
I'm already beat from helping with the move!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.210
Miss Ange, all clear.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.960
We'd better hurry.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.250
We have about 20 minutes until they get back.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.710
Miss Ange, I've been thinking.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:09:58.580
What?

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.880
What do you think about Team Wildcat?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.880
They're so swift and fearless.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.130
But they look adorable!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.540
Would you... change your voice back?

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.000
It's unsettling.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.380
How do you do, Grandmother?

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:17.790
We've not seen you since
the ceremony at the music academy.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.500
How is school?

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.330
I've made some good friends.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.920
That's good to hear.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.920
Friends can be life-long treasures.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:29.170
Yes, Grandmother.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.710
What do you think of the princess?

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:39.000
She is not what I imagined.

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:43.000
She's royalty, but she speaks to us as equals.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.960
She even tells jokes.

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.830
But none of them are very funny.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:51.880
She's full of curiosity, and always giving Ange trouble.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:52.830
Chise.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.750
I trust they don't suspect you?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.540
They removed me from the infiltration team.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:04.420
We are here to find out whether we can trust
the Kingdom or the Commonwealth.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:07.210
We must choose which to ally ourselves with.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:08.960
Yes, Sir.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:10.710
I understand.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.210
Your Majesty, I believe it's time.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.420
For what?

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.500
To discuss marriage.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:19.670
Mine?

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:22.210
We told you, it's too soon.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:26.290
Such matters can wait until after she has graduated.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:28.420
I beg your pardon, Majesty,

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:33.670
but strengthening our relationship with Moscow
will lead to the stabilization of all of Europe.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:37.330
And to that end you would have Us
sacrifice Our own granddaughter?

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:45.250
Binding our countries through marriage
will squelch the possibility of a world war.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:49.170
From here on, I go alone.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:53.380
If I'm not back in ten minutes, you go back to the others.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.170
All right.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.000
Please be careful.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:41.170
Oh?

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:42.500
Welcome back.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.420
Did you leave Ange and Beatrice?

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.330
Yeah, well, you know...

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:49.210
Will they be all right?

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.920
You're worried?

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.040
Yes, of course.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.670
This is for your ears only.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:03.830
This mission will deal a damaging blow to the Kingdom.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:09.500
If Princess is a double agent, she's sure to take action.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.210
You mean...?

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:16.290
We haven't abandoned the possibility
that Princess is our enemy.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.540
Is something the matter?

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:22.580
Oh, no. I was just wondering
what would make a good team name.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.710
Miss Ange has been gone a long time.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.540
No...

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.000
Was there a leak?

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.170
No, even if there was...

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:14.920
This is some big equipment.

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:18.670
This definitely would have been the research facility.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.290
Give me a break!

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.460
I'm already beat from helping with the move!

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.130
They moved it?

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:34.830
Up there?

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.130
This is...

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:11.580
Miss Dorothy!

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.880
Beatrice? Where's Ange?

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:17.000
She told me to leave without her
if she didn't come back in ten minutes.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.460
Really. She must be having some trouble, then.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.080
I hope she's all right.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:28.670
Come with me.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.250
Let's go, Princess.

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:33.630
What's the matter?

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.710
There's no time.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:36.080
I'll explain on the way.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.630
What's going on?

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.250
Apparently they moved the entire laboratory.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.670
Was there an information leak?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.330
I don't know.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:47.420
But I found the loading dock they used.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:49.170
It leads to the Thames.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.830
So they escaped by boat?

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:53.250
The drawbridge only opened up ten minutes ago.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.960
They can't have gotten far.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:59.710
If we take the shortest route,
we should catch up to them at Greenwich.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:00.630
Got it!

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.380
Our research was finally on the right track.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:19.080
Why should we have to move NOW?

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:22.670
In answer to your question, I'd like you to look at this.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.460
What does that book have to do with anything?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.040
You'll see.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.580
A camera?

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.170
There is a Commonwealth spy in our midst.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:39.420
We will now conduct a VERY thorough investigation.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.000
Left at the next corner.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:48.380
Right at the next intersection.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.130
Right at the next stairway.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:55.880
You got it!

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:58.080
Stairway? But we're in an automobile!

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.420
Don't bite your tongue.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:04.540
How do you feel about Team Meikyo Shisui?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.000
("Mirror-smooth Water")
How do you feel about Team Meikyo Shisui?

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:08.790
What does it mean?

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.380
Next, through that narrow passage
up ahead and turn left!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.330
Nobody fall out!

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:20.960
Be quiet.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:31.830
There it is.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:33.750
We made it!

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:38.000
I thought maybe Princess
had leaked the information, but...

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:40.040
It's quite the large boat, isn't it?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.540
At that size, it could be carrying an entire platoon.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.000
I will go with you.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.960
No. You stay here, Chise.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.000
Dorothy and I will go alone.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.080
You would leave me behind again?

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:55.710
Miss Chise...?

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.210
I'm a stronger asset than Dorothy!

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:00.130
I know.

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.460
Then why...

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:04.830
You came to us under the graces of Lord Horikawa.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.540
We can't ask you to put yourself in danger.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.130
Your concern is unnecessary!

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.750
I said I would go!

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.290
Your Highness?

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:19.250
I'm going, too.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:20.830
No, you can't!

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.330
I've been trained.

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:27.580
Besides, if I go, you won't have to leave a guard with me.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.790
Wait a minute, Princess.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.380
This isn't some party we're talking about.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.630
It's too dangerous for an amateur.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.460
I'd like to know why you're so eager to take the risk.

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:40.880
Come now, I've been in danger all along.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:44.500
If word gets out that I'm a spy, it's over for me.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:49.580
I'm standing on a precipice... a bridge much narrower
and more fragile than this one.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.500
That's no reason to put yourself in MORE danger!

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.460
It's the same either way.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:59.460
If you all fail, that will lead them directly to my secret.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.460
And in that case,

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:06.250
I must put my life on the line to make this plan succeed.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.380
If Princess is a double agent,

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:14.040
it shouldn't matter if her secret gets out-
she would have a safety net.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:17.250
There would be no reason to take such a big risk.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.960
All right, Princess.

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:24.040
We're on this boat together, then.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:26.460
Yes!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.380
What was that?

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:39.880
Did you kill him?

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.460
He wasn't strong enough to merit killing.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:44.290
What do we do now?

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:46.210
We split into two groups.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.330
Princess and I will go aft.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.460
Right. We'll take the bow, then.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:00.630
Charlotte.

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:01.880
Are you angry?

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.460
Of course I am, after that stunt...

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:05.960
I was worried sick.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.460
I'm sorry.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:11.040
Meanie. You like to see me squirm.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.420
Can you blame me, Charlotte?

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:16.170
You act like I'm the only important one.

00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:17.630
Because...

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:20.540
When we were children, you talked to me like normal.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.960
If I did that now, people would know we're old friends.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:27.460
But we're ALL friends.

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:31.710
All right, then, why don't we say
we met and realized we're kindred spirits?

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:33.920
Then we wouldn't have to hide our friendship.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.040
No.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.630
I would lose control of myself.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.380
I think it's good to let your hair down on occasion.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.040
Like you used to.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.210
I hate who I used to be.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.170
But it's the old you

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.710
that I love so much.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.670
You've finally shown your true colors.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:56.830
What?!

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:04.540
The Cavorite research team, I presume?

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.040
We'd like you to come with us.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.170
You're...

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:12.540
You can't be...

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:13.830
We are spies.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.000
We haven't settled on a name yet.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:25.750
Not only did we get the prototype,
but we have the researchers in custody.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.460
The results were even better than we hoped.

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:31.830
Now Princess is clear of all suspicion.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:32.750
No.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:35.960
This world isn't black and white.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:38.460
Only black and grey.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:40.790
And the princess is grey.

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.540
Keep a constant watch on her.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:50.670
All right, then.

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:53.170
As part of the food series, let's be Team Carrot!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.710
These are getting worse and worse.

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.630
I don't especially like carrots.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:01.250
Your Highness! You mustn't be picky!

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:08.130
I know. What about Team White Pigeon?

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:09.210
Pigeon?

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:10.750
Not bad.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:14.000
It's pretty and cute. I like it!

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:16.500
They do call spies "pigeons."

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:18.290
Really?

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:23.790
After the Flood, Noah sent a dove...
a pigeon... to scout for land.

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:25.580
Then that settles it.

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:27.540
What do you think, Miss Dorothy?

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:31.380
I like it. Team White Pigeon.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:34.460
I especially like that it's not grey.

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:36.330
I knew you'd like it!
